            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A physiologic monitoring system (100) comprising: a central hub (120); a management portal (130); at least one non-invasive peripheral device (110A) configured to measure physiologic data from a patient and in communication with said central hub (120); at least one invasive peripheral device (110B) associated with said patient and in communication with said central hub (120); wherein the central hub (120) allows for accessing a patient application (126) and further includes a reader interface module, RIM, (128), wherein the RIM (128) is configured to communicate with the at least one invasive peripheral device (110B), wherein interaction between the patient application (126) and the RIM (128) includes separate functionality as the patient application (126) is designed to communicate with the at least one non-invasive peripheral device (110A) while the RIM (128) is designed to communicate with the at least one invasive peripheral device (110B).</p>
            </abstract>
